# ─── Slesh raw exports (PII — never commit) ─────────────────────────
# Raw Slesh exports contain customer names, emails, IBANs — never commit.
# Curated extracts via Cowork are PII-stripped (no names, emails, user IDs,
# wristband tags) and ARE committed under data/sundance-{year}/ for
# version control + cross-session reproducibility.
data/*
!data/sundance-2023/
!data/sundance-2024/
!data/sundance-2025/
*.xlsx
# but DO track the Slesh event-plan fixture (Phase 4 parser tests)
!backend/tests/fixtures/excel/*.xlsx
*.xls
*.bak
backups/

# AI assistant scratch files
CLAUDE.md
**/CLAUDE.md

# ML model artifacts — committed selectively after verification.
# By default exclude .joblib; once a trained model is verified,
# `git add -f` the specific file to commit it.
*.joblib

# ML training data extracted from historical Slesh exports (Phase A,
# revenue-prediction feature). Derived from raw exports outside this
# repo (~/Desktop) — reproducible via
# backend/scripts/extract_historical_sundance.py. Not PII (no names/
# emails/user ids), but still local-only / not version controlled.
backend/scripts/ml_data/
cbw_audit/

# Day 3 demand model — raw per-line purchase rows fetched read-only
# from production (customer_key, product_name, bar_id, timestamps) for
# fast local iteration on the shape-curve fit. Same rationale as the
# ml_data/ rule above: reproducible via build_demand_training_data.py
# + a read-only prod fetch, not version controlled.
backend/app/scripts/ml_data/

# Aug-2 event clone — raw source-event dump (product names, prices,
# recipe/menu detail) fetched read-only from production by
# clone_event.py --fetch-source. Reproducible any time by re-running
# that command; not version controlled.
backend/scripts/event_clone_data/
